From 51e1b1b4abfb11d383ae23fb07bca1a1230a1e07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dustin Scott <dscott98@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:53:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: move deployment AI Gateway model setup into add
 dialog

Consolidate the deployment-managed AI Gateway catalog controls with the existing Add AI Model dialog. The providers route now supplies the admin capability to that dialog, exposes a deployment-model choice only for gateway-enabled administrators, and uses the same dialog for edits. Deployment-model row actions retain admin-only edit/remove controls, so regular users can select but not manage shared models.

This is an unavoidable upstream frontend extension: deployment model configuration depends on Workshop admin RPC capabilities and must coexist with the provider catalog. A Blueprint, Gatekeeper, or deployment configuration cannot provide that authenticated, per-deployment management UI.
